# codec-higgs_audio_v2 (third-party, unchanged)

Shared audio tokenizer for the Amharic OmniVoice variants. It uses eight codebooks
with 1,024 entries at 25 code frames per second, with 24 kHz audio.

The weights are unchanged from the upstream Higgs Audio v2 tokenizer. Their source
snapshot is recorded in the repository manifest.

- Keep this folder beside the selected `tts-codec_llm-0.6b-amh-*` folder, or supply its
  location through the inference API's codec argument.
- Always use FP32 for the codec, including with FP16 TTS weights. FP16 codec
  execution can produce invalid tokens and non-finite audio.
- The codec can run on CPU or GPU. Reference measurements were approximately
  0.8 GB of memory and 0.2–0.3 seconds per decode on a GB10; other hardware varies.

## Terms

The [Boson Higgs Audio 2 agreement](../LICENSES/Boson-Higgs-Audio-2.txt),
incorporated [Meta Llama 3 agreement](../LICENSES/Meta-Llama-3.txt), and
[NOTICE](../NOTICE) apply. See the [codec model card](../cards/codec.md).
